# Cravio — AI Food Concierge
# Cursor always reads this file first. Do not delete or rename it.

## WHAT THIS APP IS
Cravio is a mobile app that eliminates food indecisiveness by acting as an AI concierge.
Instead of clunky manual filters, the user tells the AI what they are craving in natural
language and the AI finds a real restaurant match near them. As the user builds a profile
over time, the AI learns their preferences and gets smarter with every interaction.

---

## TECH STACK
- Frontend: Flutter (Dart)
- Backend + Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- Version Control: Git
- LLM API: Gemini API (free tier for MVP — Phase 1 only)
- Restaurant Data API: Google Places API (free $200/month credit)
- Future paid option: Yelp API (Phase 2+), OpenAI API (Phase 2+)

---

## CRITICAL ARCHITECTURE RULE — NEVER VIOLATE THIS
The LLM (Gemini) NEVER generates, names, or fabricates restaurant data.
The LLM's ONLY job is to parse the user's craving into structured JSON search filters.
ALL restaurant data shown to the user (name, photo, address, price, hours, distance)
comes exclusively from the Google Places API. This prevents hallucination entirely.

Correct data flow:
  User types craving
    → Gemini interprets craving → returns JSON filters only
    → Google Places API called with those filters
    → Real, verified restaurant data displayed to user

If a user says "something spicy and cheap", Gemini returns something like:
  { "keyword": "spicy", "price_level": 1, "open_now": true, "radius": 1500 }
Google Places then handles the actual restaurant lookup. Gemini never outputs a restaurant name.

