## FEATURE DETAILS

### Location
- Default: use device's current GPS location
- User can also manually select a different location (not just where they are)

### Distance
- Distance slider/gauge is a key feature — users care deeply about this
- Options: walk / short drive / far drive  OR  0.5 mi / 1 mi / 3 mi / 10 mi
- Always factor distance into the Google Places API radius parameter

### Manual Filter Failsafe (Phase 2)
- If AI is not satisfying the user's needs, show a manual filter panel
- Filters: cuisine type, price range, distance gauge
- These are a fallback, not the primary experience

### Bookmarks (Phase 2)
- User can save a restaurant they said YES to
- Rating system: 1–5 stars per saved restaurant
- Data saved to Supabase: cuisine, restaurant price, location, where user usually eats
- Bookmark data feeds back into the AI to build preference profile over time
- Bookmarks are private by default — only visible to friends

### Friend System (Phase 3)
- Search users by username
- Send / accept / decline / remove friend requests
- Mutual friends only — no followers, no public profiles
- Friends can view each other's bookmarks (read-only)
- Can copy a restaurant from a friend's bookmark into your own

### Recs / Send to Friend (Phase 3)
- Any restaurant card has a "Send to Friend" button
- Pick a friend → they get a notification: "[Friend] thinks you'd like [Restaurant]"
- Recs show up in a Recs inbox
- Each notification shows: sender name, restaurant name, Save + Dismiss buttons inline
- Bell icon shows badge counter (red dot with number) for pending recs
- Notification panel opens as a bottom sheet or side drawer (NOT an iframe — Flutter native)

### Discounts / Deals (Future / Additional)
- When a restaurant is selected, check if there are Groupon or food service deals
- Nice-to-have, not MVP

